+
+### RBR-14 — Cross-host clocks
+
+Runner, every API replica/worker and database host must be NTP-synced. **Bound owed, owner Platform/SRE (U11).** R9-OBS2 checks `issuedAt <= Date.now()` on runner with zero tolerance; a runner clock behind the minting clock by more than mint-to-submit latency can refuse a valid grant with 409 AUTHORIZATION_EXPIRED. R9-OBS1 stamps `pending_deadline_at = acceptedAt +600s` on JVM, while dispatch judges with DB `clock_timestamp()`. Inspect actual host synchronization and the supplied bound when investigating. Do not add tolerance or lengthen the 30 s grant as a remedy. Sources: 010 AC5 clock row; 012A architect R9/R10 ruling.
